			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "86a07022d88633c1465ca55ed1054af34d55fe58"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T02:01:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				142,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Introduce manualChunks for non-bundled profile\n\nSplit the massive `partsSplash` chunk in non-bundled build profiles (e.g., debug-electron) into parallel-fetchable segments. The previous configuration kept the entire Effect-TS runtime, Wind service layer, and telemetry stack in a single file, hindering V8 parsing and browser preloading.\n\nImplement a conditional `manualChunks` strategy that isolates:\n- `effect-rt`: The Effect-TS runtime (~800 KB)\n- `wind-effect-gen`: Stable, large codegen layer\n- `sky-telemetry`: PostHog/OTLP bridges (off critical path)\n- `sky-debug`: Diagnostic harnesses\n\nCrucially, this strategy is skipped for the bundled profile. Merging chunks there would break the strict initialization order between `workbench.js` and `workbench.desktop.main.js`, causing the FS provider chain to fail due to incorrect `isElectron` mode detection.\n\nThis change optimizes load times for debug profiles while preserving the critical runtime contract required for the bundled distribution.",
			"SHA": "f11f53d5ba2325fc6e56d64ec48f2f9f0bf08920"
		}
	],
